t(54, 1300, """In the scale of our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, great in the heavens and on earth, exalted greatly, our Lord gives no weight to whoever disbelieves in Him and counts him as zero in value, even if she were the most beautiful woman in the world, of noble lineage and descent, of great intelligence and genius; she is, with Allah the Exalted, = zero, in the full sense of the word zero. And even if he were a handsome man, of great strength, a genius, a scholar in his field, the son of a family of noble name and lineage, he is, with Allah the Exalted, = zero. In contrast, every day we find those to whom Allah the Exalted gives no weight glorifying themselves on social media and saying: We, and we, and we! They look at themselves as higher than others! They even speak with (disgust) about the believers in tawhid! They come out to people saying: We are a red line, we are forbidden to touch, we will be on earth only as the mighty above everything. This is their view of themselves, but where is the truth? The truth is something else entirely. These who appear on screens, in demonstrations and in marches, and boast of their looks, appearances, origins and recent history, see themselves as something very great, but in truth, according to the real scale, they are not as they view themselves, apart from their share of the human rights guaranteed to all humans without exception.

Our Great Lord, holy are His names and attributes, says about the real value of those who refused to believe in Him and affirm His oneness:

"Those are the ones who disbelieved in the signs of their Lord and in the meeting with Him, so their deeds have become worthless, and We will not assign to them on the Day of Resurrection any weight" .. They have no weight on the Day of Resurrection, and no real weight in this world apart from their human rights.

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: "A huge, fat man will come on the Day of Resurrection and will not weigh with Allah the wing of a gnat" (narrated by al-Bukhari and Muslim).""")

